 and India. It operates in three segments: Full-Service Center-Based Child Care, Back-Up Care, and Educational Advisory services. The Full-Service Center-Based Child Care segment offers traditional center-based early education and childcare, preschool, and elementary education services. The Back-Up Care segment provides center-based back-up childcare, in-home child and senior care, school-age programs, camps, tutoring, pet care, and self-sourced reimbursed care services, as well as sittercity, an online marketplace for families and caregivers through early education and childcare centers, school-age programs and in-home care providers, the back-up care network, and other providers. The Educational Advisory services segment offers tuition assistance and student loan repayment program management, workforce education, and related educational consulting services, as well as college admissions and college financial advisory services. The company was formerly known as Bright Horizons Solutions Corp. and changed its name to Bright Horizons Family Solutions Inc. in July 2012. Bright Horizons Family Solutions Inc. was founded in 1986 and is headquartered in Newton, Massachusetts.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Stephen Howard Kramer | CEO, President & Director | Age 54 | Compensation: $1.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 32K people. Revenue per employee of $91K ranks in the bottom quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers, with revenue growing 8%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $8K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $951 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 20\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Bright Horizons Family Solution is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $2.5B market cap on $2.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +13% over the past three years and +7% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 24% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $259M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 9 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.82\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 7.0\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 8.9% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.3% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Significant goodwill (47% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 39% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Piotroski score 8/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Financial quality scores above most Consumer Cyclical peers","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Is Bright Horizons Family Solutions (BFAM) Cheap As Goodwill Write Down And Guidance Reset Land?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/consumer-services/nyse-bfam/bright-horizons-family-solutions/news/is-bright-horizons-family-solutions-bfam-cheap-as-goodwill-w","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794526401.141,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.955,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"Bright Horizons Family Solutions Inc. (NYSE:BFAM) Stock Has Consensus Target Price of $79.50 According to Brokerages","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/bright-horizons-family-solutions-inc-nysebfam-stock-has-consensus-target-price-of-79-50-according-to-brokerages.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794468656.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.888,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"The Technical Signals Behind (BFAM) That Institutions Follow","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/10/The_Technical_Signals_Behind_BFAM_That_Institutions_Follow_111026024002_1794296402.html","date":"